Prague has completed tenders for new taxi station administrators.
It receives about 12.3 million crowns per year for 103 parking spaces.
Until recently, for the same places for taxi drivers, she collected 150 thousand crowns per year.
This was reported by Councillor Lukáš Manhart (TOP 09).
Previously, the city used draws when selecting administrators.
The winner then received a lease for a flat amount of 1000 crowns per year.
However, the rules have changed.
At present, the amount of the offer decides.
"The year since the termination of the original lease agreements and the opening of the tenders, it has been proven that the new rental system is much more advantageous for Prague and fairer overall," the councillor argues.
The most expensive spot is Na Perštýně
The highest price was offered by those interested in a station in Na Perštýně street.
He pays 2.1 million crowns a year.
Approximately 1.5 million crowns the new administrators paid for the places in front of the Municipal House or on Wenceslas Square.
Councillors adopted the new rules on the rental of taxi stations in the autumn of 2012 and terminated the original leases in the summer of last year.
Tenders were held in four waves and the new administrator found 29 posts.
