Another goal without waiting?
It's not for a big celebration, admits Dvorak in Hradec Králové
We take the point and we are happy for it.
We had more chances in the first half, the second-home one," said the striker, who scored from a penalty kick this time.
Weren't you nervous when you played it, after all accompanied by a huge whistling?
I didn't particularly notice it, although on the second wicket, where there are home fans, it would probably be worse.
After half an hour, you equalized with a penalty, but you also got a goal from a penalty after less than four minutes.
What's happened?
We overslept the beginning, we were passive, it came out of the corner, and then a penalty.
After that, you stepped up and the first half you were the better team, which had more chances.
Why did that change after the break?
It's hard to tell.
I agree that we played well after the goal scored until the break.
In the booth we said we wanted to keep the pace of the game after it, but we couldn't do it.
To tell you the truth, I can't even explain why.
However, it is probably also true that the locals said something about their game during the break, they were probably not very happy with it.
You've only scored for the first time on your opponent's pitch, while maybe you haven't scored a goal at home yet.
Why is it such a difference?
I don't think it's such a difference, it's up to us how we deal with it.
We started well in Brno, but then it was bad of us, Pilsen, that's a different category.
You've been waiting for a goal for four games, weren't you worried that it might be similar after the last game?
Not really, but, of course, we're glad we don't have to talk about waiting for a goal since last game.
Now we've added more without waiting, but they're still only three in six games, which isn't for a big celebration yet.
Island - lava flows from a crater.
Lava flying to the surface in Holuhraun near the Vatnajökull glacier flows through an underground tunnel from a crater.
It is located under the glacier, as well as part of the underground lava tunnel.
This fact now worries scientists the most...
For the time being, the situation remains unchanged.
Since yesterday morning (31.8.
2014) still flies out of the crack about the same amount of lava.
Compared to the original estimates, however, its quantity is lower, not 1000 m3, but "only" 300-400 m3.
Compared to the previous eruption of 29.8.
2014 is up to 50x larger.
However, scientists fear that the lava tunnel could open even where it is located under the ice.
If this were to happen, moreover, with the same intensity as the current eruption, it would mean huge floods, both on the Jökulsá á Fjöllum and on other rivers.
There is a strong smell of sulphur around the eruption, clouds of steam and gases rise from the crack.
It is certainly not an eruption suitable for tourism, as was the case with the eruption at Fimmvörðuháls in 2010.
This is much bigger, and there's also a lot more gases," says volcanologist Ármann Höskuldsson.
However, the weather has improved considerably since yesterday, there was almost no wind in the area in the morning hours.
Traces of the sandrous storm were washed away by rain.
Scientists can continue their work.
